<Base title="Our Programs" description="Explore the four pillars of GEAR Moto Foundation: Gear, Education, Assistance, and Recovery.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Our four pillars</div><h1>Gear. Education.<br/><span class="accent">Assistance. Recovery.</span></h1><p class="lede" style="color:#e5e8eb">Four connected commitments to support riders before a crash and through the challenges that may follow.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><div class="program-pillar"><img src="/images/Gear_G.png" alt="G — Gear" loading="lazy"/><span>G · Gear</span></div><h2>Protective Gear Access</h2><p>Our proposed Gear program will help qualifying riders access essential protective equipment, including compliant helmets, armored riding apparel, gloves, and boots. Planned delivery methods include partner discounts, vouchers, donated equipment, and direct-to-vendor awards, subject to funding and approved eligibility policies.</p>
<div class="program-pillar"><img src="/images/Gear_E.png" alt="E — Education" loading="lazy"/><span>E · Education</span></div><h2>Rider Education</h2><p>Education will focus on access to new-rider training, advanced and returning-rider courses, endorsement-related education, and relevant road-safety or first-aid learning. Proposed awards will use objective, need-based criteria and approved training providers.</p>
<div class="program-pillar"><img src="/images/Gear_A.png" alt="A — Assistance" loading="lazy"/><span>A · Assistance</span></div><h2>Rider & Family Assistance</h2><p>Assistance focuses on practical help before or after challenges arise: helping riders find trustworthy resources, navigate available support services, and connect with relevant community partners. Specific Assistance services and eligibility requirements are still being developed.</p>
<div class="program-pillar"><img src="/images/Gear_R.png" alt="R — Recovery" loading="lazy"/><span>R · Recovery</span></div><h2>Recovery & Reconnection</h2><p>Recovery focuses on the consequences of motorcycle crashes. The proposed program aims to provide need-based accident-related financial relief for qualifying riders and families, potentially including uncovered medical and rehabilitation costs, deductibles or other out-of-pocket expenses, and essential hardship needs while a rider recovers. Awards will depend on approved policies, documented need, and available funding. Recovery also means rebuilding stability and well-being; no rider is expected or pressured to ride again.</p>
<div class="program-callout"><strong>Program launch status:</strong> All four pillars are in development. Applications, award amounts, selection requirements, and opening dates have not yet been announced.</div><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/contact/">Ask About GEAR</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/get-help/">Get Help Information</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
